where $u$ is displacement, $p$ is pressure, $S_i$ are phase saturations, $C_i$ are chemical/microbial concentrations, $\sigma$ is stress, $\tau$ is shear stress, $T$ is temperature, $P$ is pressure, and $S$ is salinity.

\section{Governing Equations}

\subsection{Astrophysical Gravitational Forcing}
The gravitational energy field is given by:
\begin{equation}
E = \int_V G(r,t)\, dV,
\end{equation}
where $G(r,t)$ is a time-varying gravitational field derived from astrophysical datasets.

\subsection{Geomechanics (Biot Consolidation)}
The geomechanical behavior is governed by:
\begin{equation}
\partial_t\left(\frac{p_M}{M} + \alpha \nabla\cdot \mathbf{u}\right)
= \nabla\cdot\left(\frac{k}{\mu}\nabla p\right) + Q',
\end{equation}
where $p_M$ is matrix pressure, $M$ is constrained modulus, $\alpha$ is the Biot coefficient, $\mathbf{u}$ is displacement, $k$ is permeability, $\mu$ is fluid viscosity, and $Q'$ is a source/sink term.

\subsection{Multiphase Flow (Water--Methane)}
Multiphase Darcy flow is described by:
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{v}_i = -\frac{k k_{ri}}{\mu_i} \nabla p_i,
\end{equation}
with saturation constraint:
\begin{equation}
S_w + S_g = 1,
\end{equation}
where $\mathbf{v}_i$ is phase velocity, $k_{ri}$ is relative permeability, $\mu_i$ is phase viscosity, and $S_w$, $S_g$ are water and gas saturations.

\subsection{Fracture Mechanics (Mohr--Coulomb)}
Fracture and fault failure follow:
\begin{equation}
\sigma_{\text{yield}} = C + \sigma_n \tan(\phi),
\end{equation}
where $C$ is cohesion, $\sigma_n$ is normal stress, and $\phi$ is friction angle.

\subsection{Biogeochemical Reaction--Diffusion}
Biogeochemical and microbial processes are modeled as:
\begin{equation}
\partial_t C_i = D_i \nabla^2 C_i + R_i(C_i, T, P, S),
\end{equation}
where $C_i$ is concentration of species $i$, $D_i$ is diffusion coefficient, and $R_i$ is a nonlinear reaction term dependent on temperature $T$, pressure $P$, and salinity $S$.

\section{Simulation Workflow}

\subsection{Execution Pipeline}
Each timestep in GMSS proceeds as follows:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Import astrophysical forcing.
    \item Solve geomechanical deformation.
    \item Compute multiphase flow.
    \item Evaluate fracture propagation.
    \item Solve biogeochemical reaction--diffusion.
    \item Update the unified state vector $\Psi$.
    \item Generate a zero-knowledge proof for the timestep.
    \item Write the state and proof to the global ledger.
    \item Advance the simulation time.
\end{enumerate}

\section{Cryptographic Governance}

\subsection{Homomorphic Encryption}
All physics computations are performed on encrypted state, enabling privacy-preserving simulation while maintaining full functionality.

\subsection{Zero-Knowledge Proofs}
For each timestep, a zero-knowledge proof is generated to certify that the state transition obeys the governing equations and constraints:
\begin{equation}
ZK\text{-}P(d) = \text{True}.
\end{equation}

\subsection{Ledger Integration}
Validated states and their associated proofs are written to a secure ledger, forming an immutable record of physically consistent evolution.

